  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=75,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=80.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 75-80 \\\\  & =150-80 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
